title Caravan inflight -- two documents standing at once, and the rule a supervisor keeps when it cannot know which one is true
prompt Keaton set the loop running: Standfast on reds first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The living REDS rows -- 80, 83, 84, 85 -- each carry a fix and a witness, so nothing agent-closable stands open. Ran the standing guards on metal rather than reading the ledger's word for itself: living_card_ascii_witness GREEN, witness_claim_check_witness GREEN. The e123 living-pin guard has no witness under that name in tools/, so it was not run this lap; the ASCII guard covers the same two pins for the property this round could have touched.
think Rota by lap index. Twenty-three rings stood before this one, so this is lap 24, and 24 mod 27 names active-designing/20260702-184312_the-grain-and-the-crossing.md. Deep-read it. The strand that governed this round is the one it seats plainly: a guard that cannot red guards nothing. That is why this rung disabled its own region check and watched the moved document read back as safe before trusting the green.
think The next crux was already named by the last lap's log: two documents standing at once -- whether a ring may be re-declared while a lap is in flight rather than only between laps.
think First honest question: what does in flight even mean for a serial supervisor over real processes? The spawn returns a live process and the wait blocks. So a derivation taken between those two calls is taken with the child unreaped -- and unreaped is exactly the honest word, because the supervisor genuinely does not know whether the child is mid-write or exited a microsecond ago and simply not waited on.
think That ignorance turned out to be the finding rather than a hole in the proof. A supervisor re-declaring mid-lap cannot know whether the domain it is replacing has finished, so a document must be safe under BOTH readings at once. That reframing is what makes the race a feature of the claim instead of a flaw in the test.
think The freeze follows from the argv. A child takes its grants from the words it was handed, written from the document that stood at its spawn, so a file changing on disk cannot reach it. Proven by deriving serial_cycle_succession.bron -- whose table has no birch at all -- while birch is unreaped, and watching birch carry 2 asks anyway.
think The effect is the other half. The same table refuses the NEXT spawn absolutely: a step naming birch after the swap is turned away UnknownDomain. Freeze for the running one, governance for the next one.
think Exactly one property answers to both readings: the regions may not move. Wrote serial_cycle_moved.bron as the succession with ask_bc renamed ask_bd -- shape-legal, region-illegal -- so shape alone would have waved it through and only the region check catches it.
obs The first lap RED'd honestly and taught the shape. cedar under the succession reported Unheard, because birch had spent its ring on birch->cedar, a channel the succession no longer has. That is standby's own seam cost -- a standby inherits regions and never inherits a bell -- surfacing one layer deeper, mid-lap. The lap was rewritten to wake the successor's side by name, and 4 asks came home with 2 of them carried by the retired domain.
obs The refused probe surfaced a real leak by running it. The first cut returned the RegionsMoved refusal straight from between the spawn and the wait, abandoning a child it had spawned under a document that permitted every word of it -- its output arrived after the GREEN line, which is how it was caught. A refusal at the swap refuses the successor, never the running child, so the supervisor now reaps what it started before reporting why the newer document was turned away.
obs RED path proven load-bearing before the green was trusted, per the grain's own strand. With the same_regions check disabled, the moved document read back as safe whether the replaced domain finished or is still writing -- a false clearance -- and the lap fell through to a bare OutcomeMismatch. The guard is what stands between a ring and a store nobody reads.
obs Trade-off accepted: the module repeats run_child rather than importing standby's private one, matching what gap, decline, and standby each already do in this family. The seven-word argv is the shared shape; the repetition is the family's established idiom rather than new debt.
loom witness=caravan_inflight_witness result=GREEN rings=24 swaps=1 unreaped_at_swap=1 ran_under_elder=1 asks_home=4 asserts=35 lines=676
file caravan/inflight.rye the rung -- a ring re-declared with one child unreaped beneath it, and the one property safe under both readings
file caravan/systems/serial_cycle_moved.bron the successor a supervisor must refuse: a whole ring with one arc renamed
file tools/caravan_inflight_witness.rish the witness, reading every claim natively, GREEN on metal
file caravan/README.md the rung row and the section that reads the finding in prose
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves forward; standby condensed into the prior-edges line so the card stays single-stranded
recommend keep-going the next crux is more than one lap in flight at once -- whether two children of the same ring may run concurrently, and what a document owes a supervisor holding two unreaped outcomes rather than one
